I do have to say, this confused me in the [docs](https://playwright.dev/docs/auth#reuse-authentication-state):

```
// Save storage state into the file.
await context.storageState({ path: 'state.json' });
```

Especially since the description is `The following code snippet retrieves state from an authenticated context and creates a new context with that state.`.  I couldn't figure out why the result of `context.storageState`, which seemed to be getting storage state, wasn't returning anything that could be saved in the next step.  I'm a brand new playwright user, trying to figure out how I'd handle auth that includes MFA, which is how I ended up looking at this PR.
